WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:06.009
Throughout the original eight season run of
"Dexter," Dexter Morgan made some pretty questionable

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:07.009
decisions.

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:09.240
We're looking at you, Hannah McKay.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.110
Keep watching to see if the moments you flipped
out over made the list.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.150
When leading a life fraught with compulsion
and bloodshed, there will always be moments

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.060
when things go awry.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.580
Dexter learned this rather quickly at the
start of Season 3 when tracking a drug dealer

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.230
by the name of Fred "Freebo" Bowman.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.390
Destined to be the next occupant of Dexter's
kill table, the operation to nab Freebo is

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.630
a bust as Dexter must kill an innocent man
out of necessity.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:41.730
In self-defense, Dexter kills Oscar Prado,
the younger brother of Assistant District

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.270
Attorney Miguel Prado, while Freebo escapes.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.560
Naturally, Dexter manipulates the crime scene
in an effort to frame Freebo.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.910
"I went to kill Freebo and ended up killing
a total stranger."

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.030
Dexter eventually hunts Freebo down and kills
him.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.580
Meanwhile, Miguel is also on the prowl in
an effort to seek revenge for the death of

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.680
his brother.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:08.520
When Dexter confesses to Miguel that he killed
Freebo, Miguel is relieved, and the two begin

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.969
a friendship on the foundation of murdering
criminals.

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:18.030
The ugly truth that Dexter is, in fact, Oscar's
killer takes the entire situation to another

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.030
level.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.899
It requires him to frame another man for the
act while lying through his teeth to his newfound

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:25.429
friend over the ordeal.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.659
After it's revealed that Dexter orchestrated
the arrest of Rita's ex-husband, Rita incorrectly

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:34.860
assumes that Dexter is also a drug addict.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.549
"Yes, I have an addiction."

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.270
As a result, Dexter attends Narcotics Anonymous
to continue the lie.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:47.140
While attending the meetings, he meets Lila,
who becomes his sponsor.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:52.399
Quickly, Lila demonstrates a rather manipulative
element of her personality as she coaches

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:56.119
Dexter to accept himself despite his sins.

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:02.049
While she doesn't know of Dexter's Dark Passenger,
she understands that he harbors a secret.

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:06.100
Eventually, Rita finds out about Dexter's
relationship with Lila and breaks up with

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.100
him.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.001
Later, Dexter learns that Lila also has a
strange fixation, as she is something of a

00:02:12.001 --> 00:02:16.600
pyromaniac and sets her apartment on fire
to manipulate Dexter.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.290
Eventually, she attempts to blackmail Dexter
into getting back together with her, all while

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.070
Debra learns that her real name is Lila West,
and she has a criminal history.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:31.920
Eventually, Lila kills Sergeant Doakes, an
innocent man, in an effort to protect Dexter.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.190
Simply put, Dexter should have put a stop
to her dangerous actions long ago.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.890
Sergeant Doakes always had it out for Dexter.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.910
He suspected the titular character of being
strange and likely hiding something, and he

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:45.910
wasn't wrong.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.970
In fact, he eventually learns the truth about
Dexter Morgan.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:55.810
When Doakes tries to arrest Dexter, the serial
killer overpowers the sergeant and locks him

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.310
in a cell at a remote cabin.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.860
At this point, Dexter lays it all out on the
table and tells the sergeant that he is the

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.450
Bay Harbor Butcher.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:09.150
Ultimately, Dexter commits to evading law
enforcement by framing Doakes as the serial

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.180
killer.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.520
Dexter then kills one of his targets in the
cabin in front of Doakes.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:19.330
After he witnesses the shock of the police
sergeant toward his bold crimes, he starts

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.470
reflecting on his past.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:26.510
That's when Dexter realizes that Harry actually
committed suicide because he couldn't cope

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:31.340
with his son's actions despite teaching him
the code and trying to protect him.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:36.500
The sergeant's shock reflects what Harry must've
felt, and Dexter considers doing the noble

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.870
thing, which would be turning himself in.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:44.860
Unfortunately for Doakes, Lila finds the remote
cabin and burns it to the ground with Doakes,

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.010
and any evidence proving Dexter is a serial
killer, inside.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.330
The FBI then concludes that Doakes is the
Bay Harbor Butcher, allowing Dexter to walk

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.330
free.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.320
While a moment of introspection almost leads
Dexter to do the right thing, he still originally

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.230
planned to frame an innocent man for murder.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.470
That's low, even by Dexter's standards.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:11.320
While Dexter's relationship with Rita begins
with the sole purpose of providing him with

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:16.959
the camouflage he needs to hide in plain sight,
it eventually flourishes into some form of

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:17.959
legitimacy.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:23.599
Unfortunately, however, his sociopathic nature
leads to many cringeworthy decisions early

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:25.460
in his courtship with Rita.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:31.469
One egregious example is when he plagiarizes
his marriage proposal from a killer who romanticized

00:04:31.469 --> 00:04:34.360
a non-existent relationship in her head.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.530
"My life was an unanswered question."

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.530
"Unanswered question."

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:44.949
While this killer may have been far too forthright
with her delusions of love, Dexter is the

00:04:44.949 --> 00:04:46.350
exact opposite.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:52.009
Therefore, he lifts her words and uses them
as his own when seeking Rita's hand in marriage,

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:54.860
once again, for the benefits it affords him.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:00.219
Dexter had his fair share of ups and downs,
but he always took pride in following Harry's

00:05:00.219 --> 00:05:01.580
code to the letter.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:07.590
However, during the Season 4 episode "Slack
Tide," the Miami PD is hunting for a killer

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:11.479
after finding the arm of a model inside the
belly of an alligator.

00:05:11.479 --> 00:05:16.450
This turns Dexter on to Jonathan Farrow, a
photographer who takes twisted pictures of

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:20.159
female models who all appear tortured or under
duress.

00:05:20.159 --> 00:05:23.520
"Even I'm disturbed by this."

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:28.360
Dexter becomes intent on nabbing Farrow before
the Miami PD finds the evidence that they

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.090
need to make the arrest.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.050
He gets the suspect on his infamous kill table.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:37.680
The photographer adamantly insists that he
never killed anyone and that his photographs

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.240
are merely art.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:43.259
Dexter pulls the trigger anyway and hacks
the man to death with a cleaver.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:48.570
Later, he sees Detective Batista taking Farrow's
assistant into custody and charging him with

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.379
the murder of the women.

00:05:50.379 --> 00:05:56.419
Unbeknownst to Dexter, uncovered surveillance
footage actually incriminated Farrow's assistant.

00:05:56.419 --> 00:06:01.809
Thus, Dexter was burdened with the harsh reality
that he killed an innocent man.

00:06:01.809 --> 00:06:07.360
While Dexter often lacks remorse, he demonstrates
guilt over the idea that he betrayed Harry.

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:13.870
Season 4 of Dexter is often considered the
best in the entire series, and for good reason.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:18.860
John Lithgow plays one of the most captivating
antagonists of the series in the form of the

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.550
deadly Trinity Killer.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:25.779
The murderer, Arthur Mitchell, is a tortured
soul who went through a traumatic experience

00:06:25.779 --> 00:06:29.180
equally as traumatic as Dexter's in his youth.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:34.330
As a young boy, where he witnessed the death
of his sister and the suicide of his mother.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:40.259
He also grappled with his compulsory need
to kill his abusive father at the age of 10.

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:45.449
This moment ultimately completes the trinity
killing template that Arthur uses annually

00:06:45.449 --> 00:06:47.210
with three innocent victims.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.930
"This is where it all started."

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.020
The Trinity Killer's identity as Arthur Mitchell
surprises Dexter.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:58.849
He learns that Arthur is a family man who
contributes service regularly to his local

00:06:58.849 --> 00:06:59.849
church.

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:05.000
Arthur also leads a charitable organization
known as "Four Walls One Heart," which he

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.139
uses to construct homes for the less fortunate.

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:13.210
Ultimately, Dexter quizzically wonders how
Arthur can maintain the balance of leading

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.939
two totally separate lives.

00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:22.009
Instead of killing Trinity, Dexter decides
to don the fake alias of Kyle Butler and infiltrate

00:07:22.009 --> 00:07:27.639
Arthur's congregation in an effort to educate
himself on how to better lead a normal life

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:29.960
outside of his killing rituals.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:36.460
Quickly, however, Dexter learns that Arthur
is a rather abusive father who behaves erratically.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:40.770
Maintaining a healthy balance isn't possible,
and Dexter plots to kill him.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:45.889
Of course, the Miami PD is closing in on the
killer, putting Dexter against the clock.

00:07:45.889 --> 00:07:50.669
Tragically, if Dexter had killed the Trinity
Killer when he first learned of his crimes,

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:54.240
the deaths and despair that followed wouldn't
have occurred.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:59.879
In the debut episode of Season 5, Dexter prepares
for Rita's funeral.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:04.249
After coming to grips with his own grief and
regret, he enters a convenience store and

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:08.830
crosses paths with a charming individual who
is pounding the bell at the counter for a

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:12.349
restroom key and threatening to defecate on
the floor.

00:08:12.349 --> 00:08:17.219
After reaching behind the counter and finding
the bathroom key himself, he brushes past

00:08:17.219 --> 00:08:21.369
Dexter, locking eyes with him and making an
untoward comment.

00:08:21.369 --> 00:08:26.819
Regrettably for this hot-headed fool, he spouted
off at the wrong place and time.

00:08:26.819 --> 00:08:31.570
Dexter's sense of self-control is at an all-time
low as he struggles to pick up the pieces

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.250
of his shattered life.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.479
The killer follows the man to the bathroom
and explains to him that the week hasn't been

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:40.240
kind, thanks to the death of his wife.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.839
The man makes another unsavory remark about
Dexter's deceased wife and then quickly receives

00:08:45.839 --> 00:08:49.690
several blows to the head with the blunt end
of a boat anchor.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:54.990
While the foul-mouthed vagrant was possibly
deserving of many things, insults and ravings

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:57.940
aren't exactly worthy of a death sentence.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:02.690
It's definitely not Dexter's finest moment,
and it marks the first time ever that he kills

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.579
an unvetted person solely on impulse and emotion.

00:09:07.029 --> 00:09:11.610
In Season 7 of the show, the walls are closing
in on Dexter Morgan.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.839
Captain LaGuerta is leading the charge in
a persistent effort to exonerate her late

00:09:15.839 --> 00:09:20.570
partner, Sergeant Doakes, of the Bay Harbor
Butcher name.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:25.750
Laguerta makes it frighteningly clear that
she intends to "nail Dexter to the wall,"

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:29.810
after her first attempt at arresting him goes
belly up, thanks to some careful planning

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:30.860
on Dexter's part.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:34.070
"I have proof he's the Bay Harbor Butcher."

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:39.649
Seeing that she simply won't quit, Dexter
plans the unthinkable, a premeditated murder

00:09:39.649 --> 00:09:42.320
that defies the code entirely.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:47.470
Dexter has violated the code in the past,
but the plot to kill Laguerta feels especially

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:52.589
dirty given the lengthy professional and sometimes
personal relationship the two shared over

00:09:52.589 --> 00:09:53.810
the years.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:57.980
Dexter lures Laguerta to an empty shipping
container at the docks.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:03.149
He prepares to stage a scene that makes it
look like Hector Estrada and Laguerta killed

00:10:03.149 --> 00:10:04.149
each other.

00:10:04.149 --> 00:10:11.170
Deb arrives, and as Laguerta attempts to convince
Deb to kill Dexter, Deb kills Laguerta instead.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:16.589
In an effort to protect himself and his sister,
Dexter ultimately breaks his father's code

00:10:16.589 --> 00:10:22.250
with the plot to kill an innocent police captain
while simultaneously ruining Debra's life.

00:10:23.449 --> 00:10:28.779
In Season 7, the most significant volatile
variable to enter Dexter's life is Hannah

00:10:28.779 --> 00:10:29.779
McKay.

00:10:29.779 --> 00:10:32.839
"You obviously want something, you keep making
excuses to see me."

00:10:32.839 --> 00:10:35.620
Quickly, the two share a connection.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:40.740
Her past is of particular interest to Dexter,
as she joined a controlling boyfriend on a

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.130
killing spree.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:46.180
If he were to believe Hannah's story, she
was forced into complicity.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.680
However, Dexter suspects that Hannah was just
as involved and thrilled about the killing

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.139
spree as her murderous partner.

00:10:53.139 --> 00:10:58.329
After carefully investigating, Dexter renders
Hannah unconscious, and binds her to his kill

00:10:58.329 --> 00:10:59.329
table.

00:10:59.329 --> 00:11:04.230
However, after Dexter tells her that murders
are the very thing that fuels his existence,

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:07.380
she simply tells him to do what he has to
do.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:10.180
Finding a kinship in her, Dexter cuts Hannah
free.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.810
The two then proceed to have sex on the kill
table.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.830
Despite her magnetism attracting Dexter and
her unwavering commitment to Harrison, Hannah

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:21.519
proved to be pretty unlikeable with fans.

00:11:21.519 --> 00:11:27.470
Plus, seeing Dexter succumb to Hannah's apparent
charms while she was on his table isn't exactly

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.519
what audiences expected.

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:34.360
And for a person whose soul is rather empty,
he should at least keep the kill table sacred.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:41.110
Ultimately, Rita was an unfortunate casualty
in the deadly game of cat and mouse that Dexter

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.160
played with the Trinity Killer.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:47.569
The ugly truth of the matter is that Rita's
death is on Dexter's hands for tampering with

00:11:47.569 --> 00:11:50.089
forces he couldn't comprehend.

00:11:50.089 --> 00:11:54.410
Even he didn't know what Trinity was capable
of until he was fully immersed in his fake

00:11:54.410 --> 00:12:00.259
persona as Kyle Butler, where he witnessed
Trinity's social and familial interactions

00:12:00.259 --> 00:12:01.339
firsthand.

00:12:01.339 --> 00:12:05.940
In order to protect Rita, the most obvious
choice would've been for Dexter to simply

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:09.779
never get himself involved with the Trinity
Killer in the first place.

00:12:09.779 --> 00:12:14.790
But of course, that would've made for an ultra-boring
show, and we all know that Dexter's compulsive

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:18.910
killing habits mean that he can't simply leave
things well enough alone.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:23.650
The next best option would've been to never
give in to his infatuation with the Trinity

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:26.360
Killer and his methods for leading a double
life.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:31.980
If Dexter didn't treat Arthur like some sort
of twisted mentor, maybe he could've killed

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.850
Arthur a bit earlier, before the two even
got entangled.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:40.860
Regardless, Dexter's drive to kill and his
admiration for Trinity were ultimately the

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.639
causes of Rita's death at Trinity's hands.

00:12:43.639 --> 00:12:49.740
It was a difficult lesson that Dexter had
a hard time learning, but old habits die hard.

